          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#closure_properties Closure properties
          #SerreFibrationHasRightLiftingAgainstJTopRelativeCellComplexes.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A Serre fibration has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingAcyclicCofibrations"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By general closure properties of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+and+injective+morphisms"} projective and injective morphisms
              %a{:href => "injective+or+projective+morphism#ClosurePropertiesOfInjectiveAndProjectiveMorphisms"} this proposition
              for details.
          %h3#RelationToHurewiczFibrations Relation to Hurewicz fibrations
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              is part of the condition on a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibration"} Hurewicz fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibration"} Hurewicz fibration
              is in particular a Serre fibration.
          %p The converse is false:
          #SerreFibrationsWhichAreNotHurewiczFibrations.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong (Serre fibrations which are not Hurewicz fibrations)
            %p
              An example of a generalized
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              which is a Serre fibration but not a Hurewicz fibration is given by Jeremy Brazas
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/241597/381"} here
          %p But under some regularity condition it does becomes true:
          #SerreFibrationsBetweenCWComplexesAreHurewiczFibrations.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (Serre fibrations of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibrations"} Hurewicz fibrations
            %p
              In the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} weakly Hausdorff topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complexes"} CW complexes
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibration"} Hurewicz fibration
            %p (No relationship between the covering map and the CW structures is required.)
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#SteinbergerWest84"}> Steinberger-West 84
            ) with the corrected proof due to (
            %a{:href => "#Cauty92"}> Cauty 92
            ) (pointers via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/241611/381"} here
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+Serre+fibration+between+CW-complexes+is+a+Hurewicz+fibration"} a Serre fibration between CW-complexes is a Hurewicz fibration
          %h3#long_exact_sequences_of_homotopy_groups Long exact sequences of homotopy groups
          %p
            Since Serre fibrations are the abstract
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            in the Serre-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"}> classical model structure on topological spaces
            , the following statement follows from general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            theory. But it may also be seen by direct inspection, as follows.
          #CylinderOverCWComplexIsJTopRelativeCellComplex.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi id
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{(id, \delta_0)}{\longrightarrow} X \times I
              into its standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGeneratingAcyclicCofibrations"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p First erect a cylinder over all 0-cells
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mn 0
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\underset{x \in X_0}{\coprod} D^0 &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\underset{x\in X_0}{\coprod} D^1 &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y_1
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Assume then that the cylinder over all
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has been erected using attachment from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{Top}
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the cylinder over its boundary is homeomorphic to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{n+1}
              and is like the cylinder over the cell “with end and interior removed”. Hence via attaching along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{n+1} \to D^{n+1}\times I
              the cylinder over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is erected.
          #SerreFibrationGivesExactSequenceOfHomotopyGroups.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \longrightarrow Y
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SerreFibration"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon \ast \to Y
              be any point and write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi y
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ι
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_y \overset{\iota}{\hookrightarrow} X \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} Y
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
              inclusion over that point. Then for every choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon \ast \to X
              of lift of the point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_{\bullet}(F_y, x)
                    \\overset{\iota_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_\bullet(X, x)
                    \\overset{f_\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\pi_\bullet(Y)
            %p
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
              is canonically identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_\ast
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ker(f_\ast) \simeq im(\iota_\ast)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_\ast
              is in the kernel of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
              (every sphere in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi y
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_y\hookrightarrow X
              becomes constant on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              For the converse, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha]\in \pi_{\bullet}(X,x)
              be represented by some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon S^{n-1} \to X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\alpha]
              is in the kernel of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              fits into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\alpha}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\overset{\kappa}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is the contracting homotopy witnessing that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast[\alpha] = 0
            %p
              Now since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is a lift of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mi const
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta  \;\colon\; \kappa \Rightarrow const_y
            %p as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ι
                                    %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi id
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi y
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\alpha}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\iota_n}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; D^n &amp;\overset{\kappa}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(id,1)}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{id}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\overset{(id,0)}{\longrightarrow}&amp; D^n \times I &amp;\overset{\eta}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;  \downarrow
