          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#general General
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+realization"} topological realization
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              is a Serre fibration.
          (due to
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "Quillen68"} Quillen 1968
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine99"} Goerss &amp; Jardine 1999, Thm. 10.10
          %h3#empty_bundles Empty bundles
          %p
          #EmptyBundlesAreSerreFibrations.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+bundles"} empty bundles
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
              %br/
              All
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+bundles"} empty bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∅
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varnothing \longrightarrow B
              are Serre fibrations, because none of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+squares"} commuting squares
              that one would have to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lift in
              actually exist:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ¬
                                %mo ∃
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∅
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D^{n} &amp;\overset{ \not \exists }{\longrightarrow}&amp; \varnothing
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    D^n \times I &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; B
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    }
            %p
              since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+topological+space"} empty topological space
              is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+initial+object"} strict initial object
              %em no
              morphism to it from any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+space"} inhabited space
            %p
          %h3#FiberBundles Fiber bundles
          %p
          #FiberBundlesAreSerreFibrations.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
                are Serre fibrations)
              %br/
              Every topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
              (i.e.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial"} locally trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              it becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+space"} product
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
          %p
            This follows immediately from Lemma
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MapIsSerreFibrationIfLocallySo"}
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+bundles"} empty bundles
            of Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmptyBundlesAreSerreFibrations"}
            are examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial"} locally trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
            (with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typical+fiber"} typical fiber
            the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+topological+space"} empty topological space
          %h3#covering_spaces Covering spaces
          #CoveringSpaceIsSerreFibration.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
                projection is Serre fibration)
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+space"} covering space
              projection is a Serre fibration, in fact a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+fibration"} Hurewicz fibration
              (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "covering+space#HomotopyLiftingPropertyOfCoveringSpaces"} this prop.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre spectral sequence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Quillen68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometric realization of a Kan fibration is a Serre fibration
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1968-019-06/S0002-9939-1968-0238322-1"} doi:1968-019-06/S0002-9939-1968-0238322-1
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1968-019-06/S0002-9939-1968-0238322-1/S0002-9939-1968-0238322-1.pdf"} pdf
            %li#SteinbergerWest84
              %p
                M. Steinberger and J. West,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Covering homotopy properties of maps between CW complexes or ANRs
            %li#Cauty92
              %p
                R. Cauty,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sur les ouverts des CW-complexes et les fibrés de Serre
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Mitchell"}> Stephen Mitchell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Serre fibrations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://sites.math.washington.edu/~mitchell/Atopc/serre.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MitchellSerreFibrations.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#tomDieck2008
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Algebraic topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ems-ph.org/books/book.php?proj_nr=86"} doi:10.4171/048
            %li#GoerssJardine99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/19990208220238/http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/simp-sets/"} webpage
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
